[
    {
        "text": "While NFT usage in the virtual world is already flourishing. Another exciting use case of NFTs is the tokenization of real world assets. These NFTs can represent fractions or collections of real world assets that can be stored and traded as tokens on a blockchain. This could introduce some well needed liquidity to many markets that otherwise wouldn't have much liquidity, such as fine art, real estate, and rare collectible items. For example, a person may want to buy a piece of physical art to sell later, but lives on a different continent from where the artwork is currently stored. Instead of packing, moving, finding a new storage facility, and unpacking the artwork, an NFT certificate of ownership can be minted and transferred to the new owner and along with it, the responsibility for paying for ongoing storage. Easy and trustless transfers of these assets could reduce friction in the global economy.",
        "start": 320,
        "end": 52620,
        "confidence": 0.9865888,
        "channel": null,
